<h2>How to combine these ideas into one plan</h2>

<p>The ideas above work best as layers rather than a shopping list. A good sequence for most Texas homes looks like this:</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Pick two or three focal points.</strong> Usually the facade, the largest tree and the front entry.</li>
  <li><strong>Add safety lighting.</strong> Paths, steps and the driveway, so guests can find their way without glare.</li>
  <li><strong>Fill the middle ground.</strong> A few beds or smaller trees so the yard has depth.</li>
  <li><strong>Extend into the backyard.</strong> Patio layers, pool surround and any water features.</li>
  <li><strong>Tie it together with controls.</strong> Zones, dimming and an astronomical timer.</li>
</ol>

